5. Editor restart under a held session: the client recovers by itself, no /mcp needed. After "r ue" (editor down at +0.2 s, up again 17.6 s later) the next call_tool got {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"error":{"code":-32600,"message":"Unknown session id '...' for 'tools/call'; client should reinitialize"}}; the client logged "MCP session expired (server no longer recognizes session ID), triggering reconnection", reinitialized in 31 ms and completed the same tool call (returnValue false); the model saw no error. Two more calls later also succeeded.
Editor down at agent start: the opposite. init reports unreal-mcp "status": "failed" (ECONNREFUSED); the client tries 4 times within ~6 s, then logs "Retry: 1 remote server(s) still failed after all retries: unreal-mcp" and never tries again. The editor came up 20 s later; in the next three turns the server stayed "failed" and the model had no mcp__unreal-mcp__* tool at all (answered NO_TOOL). A headless session has no /mcp, so it stays without Unreal MCP for its whole life; interactively /mcp would be the way back. So the agent must start after the server answers.

6. The approve payload Claude Code sends for one call_tool call, verbatim:
{"tool_name": "mcp__unreal-mcp__call_tool", "input": {"toolset_name": "EditorToolset.EditorAppToolset", "tool_name": "IsPIERunning", "arguments": {}}, "tool_use_id": "toolu_01VNm6dbGTE9Ai9nhx7TGdLK"}
(for list_toolsets: {"tool_name": "mcp__unreal-mcp__list_toolsets", "input": {}, "tool_use_id": "..."}). unreagent's approve reads tool_name and input, so it matches; for tool-search mode the inner toolset and tool sit in input, and a rule on mcp__unreal-mcp__call_tool covers every toolset tool at once.
